		(uuid "83d727f5-8df7-4998-af55-1eec0130d17d")
	)
	(text "${##}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 363.22 286.8422 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify top)
		)
		(uuid "ccc28457-2ae2-4e5f-bf7d-752604a0c11e")
	)
	(text_box "Feedback divider for 3.3V rail. Vref = 0.8 V (TPS62933F internal bandgap). R_FBT = ((Vout - Vref) / Vref) * R_FBB. R_FBB = 10 kOhm is the datasheet recommendation (10.2.2.2) -- lower values waste current at light load, higher values become noise-susceptible.  Place @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}RBMAHYAW\",\"ObjectType\":2}/ @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}BDYYQQVP\",\"ObjectType\":2} directly at the FB pin with a short trace."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.96 151.2062 0)
		(size -40.64 26.416)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ebb5a1d-6066-42bb-9725-27104c13b626")
	)
	(text_box "Input bypass per TPS62933F datasheet 10.2.2.9. @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}BMXZHHZA\",\"ObjectType\":2} (100 nF) MUST be placed directly across the VIN and GND pins with the shortest possible trace -- this is the high-frequency loop and is the single most layout-critical component on the buck. @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}YSGNGDVI\",\"ObjectType\":2} and @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}ARDAPDKC\",\"ObjectType\":2} (10 uF) is the bulk input cap.  Both rated 35V or higher to allow the X7R DC bias derating headroom against VOUT_PP peaks of ~\n8V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.74 88.7222 0)
		(size -60.96 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3066b513-c0f6-4779-9077-4503963b7c3f")
	)
	(text_box "@{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}BFRQMXYZ\",\"ObjectType\":2} is the bootstrap cap -- provides gate drive for the high-side FET.  100 nF X5R 16 V minimum, placed directly between BST and SW pins per datasheet 10.2.2.5.  Do NOT substitute X7R 0.1 uF in a different package; matching the example design avoids loop-area surprises."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 121.92 88.7222 0)
		(size -40.64 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d3556ff-c8a0-4f2d-bdae-8d335fd64312")
	)
	(text_box "@{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}OINNZFRQ\",\"ObjectType\":2} sets soft-start time. tSS = (Css * Vref) / Iss = (33 nF * 0.8 V) / 5.5 uA ~~ 4.8 ms. Datasheet 10.2.2.4 minimum is 6.8 nF.  Soft-start prevents inrush surge into the LTC4162 PowerPath when the regulator first enables."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 142.0622 0)
		(size -35.56 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "707e7276-f051-4cc0-a4f5-16b6196ed610")
	)
	(text_box "EN UVLO divider: VSTART ~~ 5.5 V rising, VSTOP ~~ 5.0 V falling. Backstop against deep-discharge oscillation if the LTC4162 LVD ever fails to disconnect the load.  Calculated per TPS62933F datasheet 9.3.6 equations 3 and 4. @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}LQGVTWZJ\",\"ObjectType\":2} and @{\"Id\":\"ERUZHJL~{K}VNBSLBVP\",\"ObjectType\":2} are SHARED betwee U2 and U3 (single divider , both EN pins tap the same midpoint) -- the EN hysteresis currents are summed and the resulting threshold shift is well within budget for this conservative target."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 170.0022 0)
		(size -43.18 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "73127575-6daa-421f-926d-c56eeb8da868")
	)
	(text_box "Feedback divider for 5V rail.  Same Vref/equation as the 3.3V stage.  Datasheet Table 10-2 lists R_top = 52.5 KOhm for this rail; 52.3 KOhm is the closest 1% standard value and gives 4.984 V output.\n\nR_FBT = ((5.0 - 0.8) / 0.8) * 10 kOhm\nVOUT = 0.8 * (1 + 52.3 / 10) = 4.984 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 378.46 153.7462 0)
		(size -40.64 26.416)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "748b6989-bd3a-4e4e-aef1-712881984432")
	)
	(text_box "REGULATION -- Both rails are produced by TPS62933F 3A synchronous buck converters fed from V_OUT_PP (LTC4162 PowerPath output, 6-18V). The TPS62933F has a 3.8-30V input range, which comfortably accepts the full PowerPath swing from battery-only (~~6V) to peak solar charging (~\n8V), perserving proper PowerPath topology.\n\nWhy TPS62933F (forced CCM variant) over the standard TPS62933: - Fixed swingtching frequency at all loads (no PFM transitions) - Predictable EMI spectrum -- imporant since the comms board peer is RF-sensitive at 145 MHz and 437 MHz - Lower output ripple under light load - Cost: ~~30% the price of TPSM5D1806, no LDO needed for 5V rail"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 27.7622 0)
		(size -119.38 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ca412d57-cc3f-4460-956b-bff9f566f068")
	)
	(text_box "PGOOD: the TPS62933F variant (SS pin) does not provide a PGOOD output.  If a power-good telemetry signal is required for the flight controller, swap one or both stages to TPS62933P (PG pin) and route an open-drain PGOOD net to Sheet 3.  For the prototype, the LTC4162's I2C telemetry already exposes input/charger health and is the primary monitoring path."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 220.8022 0)
		(size -48.26 25.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eb458e4f-bd7c-4e45-a8f9-6c504305c4d8")
	)
	(text_box "Common switching frequency choice: 500 kHz, set by floating the RT pin (datasheet Table 9-1). Rationale: 500 kHz is the lowest standard setting and gives the best efficiency, lowest switching losses, and the cleanest fundamental away from any sensitive basebands.  The two converters are not synchronized -- the RP2040 GPIOs on the flight-controller and comms boards filter their own supply locally, so beat tones between the two buck stages are not a concern.\n\nCommon feedback equation: R_FBT = ((VOUT - 0.8) / 0.8) * R_XFBB, with R_FBB = 10kOhm recommended (datasheet Equation 1, 10.2.2.2).\n\nCalculation (datasheet 10.2.2.2): R_FBT = ((3.3 - 0.8 ) / 0.8)  * 10 KoOhm = 31.25 kOhm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 27.7622 0)
		(size -91.44 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.397 1.397)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fcdf27b9-cdfb-4d14-ad92-6a496ef7e92d")
	)
